      "card_ids": ["C13"],
      "claim": "PET studies in pig and baboon showed specific, reversible striatal uptake of [11C]MP-10, confirming robust BBB penetration across species for the closest analogue.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C09"],
      "claim": "A close pyrazole-pyridinyl-phenyl-OCH2-heteroaryl analogue showed striatal brain uptake in rat biodistribution studies, supporting CNS penetration for this scaffold.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "MW150, a related pyridinyl-substituted heteroaryl compound, had a rat brain/plasma ratio >0.9, providing direct evidence that this chemotype distributes across the BBB.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C12"],
      "claim": "A lower-similarity methylpyridine analogue showed low brain-to-plasma ratio, but its polar pyridazinone/piperidine scaffold is structurally distant from the query and does not override the strong positive evidence.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is a close analogue of CNS-penetrant MP-10 and shares the pyrazolyl-pyridinyl-phenyl ether scaffold with multiple brain-penetrant compounds; direct PET and biodistribution evidence in monkeys, pigs, and rats supports meaningful CNS access. The single low-penetration analogue is structurally distant and outweighed.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct brain/plasma or CSF measurement for the exact query molecule.",
    "P-gp/BCRP efflux liability was not directly assessed for the query.",
    "The N-fluoroethyl and dimethylpyridine substituents could alter transporter recognition relative to MP-10."
  ],
